Z||000007||JSocha||05-10-2001||04:43 PM||||My feelings on this "Possible answer to gas prices?":<P>1)  Since the US of good old A is protecting the OPEC leaders with our troops, I feel we should pull out and let them fend for themselves for awhile or at least put the threat there so they get the picture not to back door us when ever they feel like it.<P>2)  But I feel, our beloved (did I say that?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> ) Gov. has their hand in the cookie jar right along with OPEC as well and is benefitting as well from the higher prices we all have to pay and will eventually pay in the future.  <P>Therefore, why would our Gov want to change anything, especially if they maybe benefiting from it.<P>They (OPEC/Our Gov) have us over a barrel and relize it as a fact "what are we (gen pub/pop) going to be able to do about it?"  Ride our bicycles 60+ miles each direction to work in protest??<P>Reminds me of the movie with Steven Segal "On Deadly Ground".  Really wonder how much truth is in his movie in his statements at the end.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by JSocha (edited 05-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||beer_stud_21||05-10-2001||05:20 PM||||All this stuff about high oil prices, lights goin out in Cali....  We're payin 2bucks a gallon for regular here in hawaii..  Have been for at least a year.  I just saw something on the news the other night that BIC (makes a$$ loads of pens and lighters etc) is about to have their raw material costs go up something like 100+%.  The sad thing about all this is we have had a great alternative to petro for the last 70 years, only problem is our stupid government is so corrupt it will never be legalized until we flat run out of crude oil on this earth.  The answer:  HEMP and for anyone here who is scared to death of Marijauana- Hemp and Marijauana are not the same thing, The plants look the same but smoking hemp to get high would be about like puttin a poppy seed muffin in your pipe when your out of cocaine.  Hemp can be grown on something like 80% of the usable land in this country, requires essentually no pestisides to grow, produces something like 250% more fiber per acre than trees do, is a renewable resource (takes a few months to mature instead of 100 yrs like the trees we have been cutting down for the last 200 years) And the oil that is extracted from the seeds can be turned into plastic and even fuel.  Henry Ford devoloped a proof of concept car that was made of resin and hemp fiber.  Plastic body panels WAY before the fiero.  This was in the mid 20's I believe.  Makes me so mad! - special interests will keep it illegal for absolutely as long as possible so that they can continue to ream the american public out like a mayson jar.  I'm sure Baby Bush wouldn't be where he is today if his daddys oil company went bust when our country, and the rest of the world for that matter decided to use an environmentally friendly and renewable resource instead of paying through the nose for something we dont even need!<P>-OK, well I'm in a contriversial mode today I guess, I was posting in the O/T section about how sensitive our country is becomming.  Oh, and I would like to appologise to any republicans that are on the forum ahead of time.  Nothing personal- I even agree with some of the things bush has to say- and he is not responsible for this problem.  But you have to admit he is of less than average intillegence.  Just listen to him talk.  He sounds like he is talking to the country as if we are bunch of second graders.  <P>sorry for the spelling errors if there are any.  I don't think the spell check works on mac.<P>-Marlin||||reg||8
