Z||000011||Voytek||05-10-2001||06:10 PM||||Not a republican here.  Not even an American, for that matter.<BR>BUT:  George Bush has nothing to do with the prices at the pump.  True enough, we up here also hope that your guys get tough with OPEC.<BR>BUT: OPEC is only in PART responsible for the prices at the pump.  Have you checked the price per barrel lately?  3 years ago, when price per barrel was about $32 USD, we were paying about 10-12 C (about 60 C per gallon USD) per liter less than we are today.  What's the price per barrel today, you ask?  Well, it's only about $27-28 bucks.  So how come we're being raped every time we fill up?  IT'S THOSE FU**ING BASTARD EXECUTIVES RESTING THEIR BIG FAT ASSES IN THEIR HEATED LEATHER CHAIRS IN THEIR CLIMATIZED OFFICES WITH WEE-WEE WIPING DUDES IN THEIR WASHROOMS.  Has anyone noticed that for the last year or 1.5 years ALL of the oil companies have been posting RECORD profits EVERY quarter??!!  If oil was REALLY costing them THAT much from the middle east, their profits wouldn't have changed that much, right?<BR>One of these days angry people are going to start filling up for 'free' and lynching those fu**ers and I'll be there...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||beer_stud_21||05-10-2001||06:37 PM||||GO VOYTEK!!!!!!!!!<P>I want to see Canada start growing tons of hemp.  I think that is about the only way to get popular opinion in the us to back hemp in this country.  Right now there is just to much money payin people to keep it illegal.  I know there are already some medium sized hemp growers up there.  I hope it works out for them.<P>-Marlin||||reg||1
